# Cat Carrier (Black Tabby) from the Dalaran mages: the rare Dalaran
# Spellscribe at Ambermill, and the Shield Guards, Theurgists and Summoners
# around Dalaran.
# Sources: items.json and the TDB's loot (Dalaran Spellscribe 16.8%; Dalaran
# Shield Guard and Theurgist 0.18%, Summoner 0.2%; Classic drop data);
# npcs.json (spawns, levels; the Spellscribe is a rare at one spot); Forever
# client 1.60.1.70532 (name; it can be traded).
# Our data marks these mages friendly to the Alliance, so this guide is Horde
# only; Alliance players buy it on the Auction House.
# ASSUMED: The Spellscribe comes back hours after a kill (Classic flow; the
# TDB's 38000-second respawn is Classic data). In-game check: how often it is
# up at Ambermill.

step Dalaran mages
  tip The Dalaran Spellscribe, a rare level 21 mage at Ambermill in southern Silverpine Forest, drops the Black Tabby about once in 6 kills. It has a single spot and can take hours to come back, so check it whenever you pass. While it is down, the Dalaran Shield Guards, Theurgists and Summoners (level 31-35) at the Dalaran crater, where Alterac Mountains meet Hillsbrad Foothills, drop it too, but only about once in 500 kills. The cat can be traded: look at the Auction House as well.
  collect 8491 "Cat Carrier (Black Tabby)" @63.5,63.3 -- Dalaran Spellscribe, Ambermill
